<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Act of Settlement 1701</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1701">1701</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Act of Settlement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Act of Settlement 1701 is an Act of the Parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> that settled the succession to the English and Irish crowns on Sophia, Electress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, and her Protestant descendants, excluding Catholics. Passed after the death of Princess Anne's last surviving child, it brought George I to the throne in 1714. It also strengthened Parliament and the independence of judges, and still governs the British succession.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701.jpg" alt="Act of Settlement 1701" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_England_(1694%E2%80%931702).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
